    "created_at": "2020-12-11T10:17:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-12-11T11:17:42Z",
    "body": "AFAIK no other browsers modify the accessibility tree for `UL/LI` based on heuristics, would it not be better to put this into the [HTML acc API spec](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) as it is concerning the exposure of role information in the acc tree?\r\n\r\nThere does appear to be a difference in how screen readers expose lists to users based on whether `list-style-type:none` is set",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
